please welcome gold medalist Ruth  Furtick group the student academy award  is an incredible honor not only because  it validates the work that went into  this film but also because it recognizes  the strength of my grandmother's words  and the power of her story by committing  that story to paper she ensured that it  would not be forgotten and that my Ann's  short life would not be lost to history  I'm very proud that by committing this  their story to film I now share a part  in preserving the legacy I'd like to  thank the academy that's just fun to say  not only for the award itself but also  for the inspiration and motivation that  comes with it to continue to do good  work I'd also like to thank several  people for their time talent and  dedication on this film Jeanne Stern for  her beautiful animation Erin wrath Aaron  wrath for his visual effects and his  much-needed morale support lodi Knoller  whose narration brought my grandmother's  words to life my parents jaan and Dina  fertig who wore many hats during the  making of this film acting as  translators archival researchers and  camera assistants the rest of my family  in America in Israel and everyone else  who worked on the film including courtly  Courtney hayslett and larga chard my  peers in the MFA film production program  at the University of Texas and finally  the faculty and staff at UT whose wisdom  and technical expertise helped me get  from the kernel of an idea to a finished  film especially Matthew Jacobs Diane  Xander Mason Ellen's bureau Charles  Ramirez Berg Suzanne craft and Louis and  my thesis committee chair Paul Steckler  thank you
 

